          "title": "You'll want to know: خرطوم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خرطوم — kharṭūm — \"a hose\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خرطوم (kharṭūm) is built on the native Arabic root kh-r-ṭ-m, \"the fore part of the nose; a trunk\" (Lane). Lane's kharṭūm is the fore part of the nose, and an elephant's trunk; the hose is a modern sense."
            }
          ]
        },
